      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Here my reaction: I know Steam has very nice VR drawing programs. For example ViveSpray. You can use your VR equipment to draw nice on the wall. Which means you don't really need tablet for it. VR worked very well as drawing equipment.\nSure tablet has pen pressures but you can control it with touchpads on controllers to make it thick and thin. And on other hand you can choose brushes, colors and more.\n\nUnless you have poor tracking, well, yes... you cannot draw nice lines. Make sure your tracking is good so you can draw good lines.\n\nAt other side, we can make good worlds focused on painting / drawing. Then you don't need really tablet because these worlds have many options to draw everything. That is much better idea.\n\nOtherwise you muse use PC without VR connected, to draw purely on mouse mode. But this will cause rounded drawings which is less nice for others. Flat is only possible with VR.",
